  "keyFeatures": [
    "Capability-based filesystem sandboxing via the Dir type — all file access is relative to an open directory handle",
    "Path traversal protection (CWE-22): blocks '..', absolute paths, and symlinks that escape the sandbox",
    "Capability-based networking via the Pool type — connections only to explicitly permitted addresses",
    "Drop-in std-like API: mirrors std::fs, std::net, and std::time with capability wrappers",
    "High-performance: uses openat2 on Linux 5.6+, O_RESOLVE_BENEATH on FreeBSD 13.0+",
    "UTF-8 path support via cap_std::fs_utf8 and the camino crate",
    "Extension traits (cap-fs-ext, cap-net-ext, cap-time-ext) for advanced operations beyond std",
    "Foundation of the WASI implementation in Wasmtime",
    "Cross-platform: Linux, macOS, FreeBSD, Windows, and WASI"
  ],
  "publicApiSurface": [
